# ── Caddy cutover: cv.javierbriceno.com → port 8000 ──────────────────────────
#
# Current (before cutover):
#   cv.javierbriceno.com {
#       root * /opt/cv-assistant
#       file_server
#   }
#
# After cutover (swap the static file_server block for this):
#
cv.javierbriceno.com {
    reverse_proxy localhost:8000
}
#
# Steps:
#   1. Start the Python app:
#        cd /opt/cv-assistant
#        docker compose up -d --build
#
#   2. Verify health:
#        curl http://localhost:8000/api/health   # → {"status":"ok"}
#
#   3. Swap the Caddyfile block above into your live Caddyfile.
#
#   4. Reload Caddy (zero-downtime):
#        caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#        # or: systemctl reload caddy
#
#   5. Confirm HTTPS is working:
#        curl https://cv.javierbriceno.com/api/health
#
#   6. (Optional) Remove the old JS frontend once satisfied with the new UI.
